"""Reviewed natural wording for trigger (condition) keys that the game does not phrase itself (docs/EFFECTS-LABELS.md).

LABELS[key] = (zh, en) or (zh, en, zh_negative, en_negative): the positive sentence of a `key = yes` condition. The negative of
`key = no` is derived from the first word (是 -> 不是, 拥有 -> 没有, 能够 -> 无法; is -> is not, has -> does not have, can -> cannot ...)
unless written out. `{loc_key}` is replaced by the game's own name of that localisation key (civic, origin, tradition ...);
effects_data.py keeps every such key. Templates of conditions with arguments use `{o}` (the named objects), `{n}` (the number)
and `{op}` (more than / at least ...; 超过 / 至少 ...).
"""
